        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: delete dead infra and config exports",
        "body": "Related: #105595\n\nAI-assisted: implemented and reviewed with Codex.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe enforced production-mode Knip ratchet still carried 593 dead-export entries under `src/config` (214) and `src/infra` (379). Those exports unnecessarily enlarged internal module surfaces and kept tests coupled to code that production never imports.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis removes export modifiers where implementations remain useful internally, deletes code and tests that existed only for dead exports, and keeps production/config contracts that are consumed by runtime callers, schema generation, or documented surfaces. Tests retained for meaningful behavior now exercise production APIs instead of re-exported test helpers. The dead-export baseline was regenerated against the final `main` merge base immediately before push.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended runtime or config behavior change. The internal TypeScript surface is smaller, dead test-only code is gone, and the enforced baseline drops every `src/config` and `src/infra` entry so future regressions are blocked by CI.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports:update` on final-base Testbox `tbx_01kxcvtqn5swmrs30z26xax06n`: 4,900 entries; generated blob `6bfd4f6bc5bc20b8267741daac502583d9a68328`, byte-identical to the pushed file.\n- Baseline verification: zero entries beginning `src/config/` or `src/infra/`.\n- Focused Testbox proof: 562 tests passed, 1 platform-specific skip across config env/session caches, promotion parsing/feed persistence, path safety, restart/reload behavior, gateway methods, and gateway E2E.\n- Final pushed-head `pnpm deadcode:exports` and `pnpm plugin-sdk:surface:check`: passed. `pnpm tsgo:prod` is blocked by an unchanged `main` error in `extensions/imessage/src/monitor/conversation-repair.ts`; the branch copy is byte-identical to merge-base `d9623bd46f3` (`44f7c8b01a617c15c30fe20cf2e24f7b71c4dbea`). Production and script TS gates passed on the immediately preceding merge base.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`: clean.\n",
